          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p Beware that there is no room to record the further possible errors of 2 qbits flipping at once. Instead, this error process takes pure qbits to one of the subspaces reserved for single bit flips. Similarly, if all three bits flip at once, the initial pure state remains in the subspace reserved for pure states, but now with its phases mixed up. Therefore, the following error correction code fails on flips of more than one of the 3-qbits and will reduce the overall error probability only if single bit flips are sufficiently more likely than double and triple spin flips.
          %p The error correction now proceeds by:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Performing a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
                of the above error syndrome
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                on the logical Qbit space. While this measurement
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state+collapse"} collapses
                the quantum state onto the subspace
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi DisturbedQBit
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DisturbedQBit_s
                the particular logical qbit states of the pure form
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PureLogicalQBit"} (1)
                lose no information under this collapse, in that there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi DisturbedQBit
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DisturbedQBit_s
                which turns any such collapse state back into the original qbit state.
            %li
